double quotes in error messages: raise ValueError('capacity must be non-negative integer') uses single quotes, so fine. But we have a lambda with double quotes? Actually the lambda uses single quotes for keys. So all quotes inside are single quotes, which are fine in JSON (since JSON string delimiters are double quotes, single quotes are literal). So only issue is newlines and backslashes (none). We need to convert actual newlines to \\n.\n\nI'll produce a properly escaped JSON string.\n\nBetter to generate it programmatically, but we'll do manually.\n\nWe can write the code as a single line with \\n inserted. Let's do that.\n\nFinal answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1726,"completion_tokens":3199,"total_tokens":4925,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1664},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2776},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1664,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":62},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}